<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Korean. English in res/values is the fallback for anything missing here.

    Korean is short and syllable-blocked, so these sit comfortably inside the
    fixed-height controls. Where Korean needs a particle it is attached to the
    word before it with a space, which is why phrases here are built per word
    rather than assembled from fragments.

    Rendering note: Poppins carries no CJK glyphs. See
    ui/theme/LocalizedType.kt - the bundled family is used when it covers the
    script and the system CJK family takes over when it does not, so these
    strings never fall back to tofu boxes.
-->
